<title>UK: INTERVIEW-British Energy sees fuel savings.</title>
<headline>INTERVIEW-British Energy sees fuel savings.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's nuclear power generator British Energy Plc said on Wednesday its new 1.5 billion stg service contract with British Nuclear Fuels (BNFL) would reduce its fuel costs by around 10 million stg this year.</p>
<p>Output this year is unlikely to match last year's level as seven statutory outages are planned at its nuclear power stations in the current year, against four the previous year, chief executive Robert Hawley told Reuters in an interview.</p>
</text>
